FINAL ANSWER:
Surviving code in this repo is mostly Troy Goode's and Douglas Christopher Wilson's, not Fiona Formatter's.

Plain `git blame` credits Fiona Formatter with 51% of the lines. That number is wrong. Their only commit, `62628c0` (2026-04-12), reformatted four files to 4-space indent and double quotes. It changed no logic but took over blame for 1016 lines.

I re-ran blame with `-w --ignore-rev 62628c0`, which skips that commit and whitespace changes. Here are the results across 1993 lines in 18 files:

| Author | Lines | Share | Last commit |
|---|---|---|---|
| Troy Goode | 746 | ~37% | 2026-04-10 |
| Douglas Christopher Wilson | 645 | ~32% | 2021-09-07 |
| Íñigo Marquínez Prado | 95 | ~5% | 2024-05 |
| Jon Church | 72 | ~4% | 2026-01 |
| Sebastian Beltran | 67 | ~3% | 2025-07 |
| Ignacio Mangas | 54 | ~3% | 2025-12 |
| Ulises Gascón | 52 | ~3% | 2026-01 |
| Eric di Domenico, Alejandro Caravaca Puchades, Linus Unnebäck, Alberto Leal | 106 combined | ~5% | — |
| Everyone else | the remaining ~100 | ~5% | — |

- **Core code:** Troy Goode and Douglas Christopher Wilson wrote most of `lib/index.js` and `test/test.js`. Troy Goode is the larger owner after the reformat is skipped. `lib/index.js` shows Troy Goode at 20 of 238 lines when the reformat is counted, so the reformat hides much of their work.
- **Config and docs:**
  - Wilson owns most of `HISTORY.md`, `LICENSE`, `package.json` and `.eslintrc.yml`.
  - Troy Goode owns most of the README and test fixtures.
  - The `.github/` workflow files belong to Íñigo Marquínez Prado, Sebastian Beltran, Ignacio Mangas and Ulises Gascón.
- **Inactivity:** `knowledge_risk` flags every file as orphaned because nobody with a commit since 2026-04-22 owns more than 50% of any file. The last commit in the repo is 2026-04-12, so this reflects a quiet repo more than anyone leaving. Wilson's last commit was 2021, so their code has been unmaintained longest.
- **Copied code:** `-w` ignores whitespace only. I did not run copy detection (`-C`), so code moved between files is credited to whoever moved it.

The commit counts point the same way: Wilson has 143 commits and Troy Goode 95. The surviving-line ranking is the reverse, with Troy Goode first. That is probably because Troy Goode's later work (tests, README) replaced older lines.

